------------------\n#### 2.  Construction for any \\(k\\le n-2\\)\n\nFix an integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**(a) Non\u2011sunny lines.**  \nTake the vertical line  \n\n\\[\nL_v:\\;x=1,\n\\]\n\nand the horizontal lines  \n\n\\[\nL_h^{(j)}:\\;y=j\\qquad (j=1,2,\\dots ,n-k-1).\n\\]\n\nThese are \\(1+(n-k-1)=n-k\\) distinct lines, all non\u2011sunny.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**(b) Sunny lines.**  \nDefine the set  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal I_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathcal T_n\\mid b\\ge n-k\\}.\n\\]\n\nIf \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal I_n\\) then  \n\n\\[\na\\le n+1-b\\le n+1-(n-k)=k+1 .\n\\]\n\nHence \\(a\\in\\{1,2,\\dots ,k+1\\}\\).  \nFor each \\(a\\ge2\\) there is exactly one admissible \\(b\\), namely \\(b=n+1-a\\).  \nConsequently  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal I_n=\\{(1,n),\\;(2,n-1),\\;(3,n-2),\\dots ,(k+1,n-k)\\}.\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nThe point \\((1,n)\\) already lies on the vertical line \\(x=1\\); the remaining \\(k\\) points  \n\n\\[\nP_i=(i+1,\\;n-i)\\qquad (i=0,1,\\dots ,k-1)\n\\]\n\nare distinct.\n\nChoose \\(k\\) pairwise different real numbers  \n\n\\[\nm_0,m_1,\\dots ,m_{k-1}\\notin\\{0,\\infty,-1\\}.\n\\]\n\nFor each \\(i\\) define the line  \n\n\\[\n\\ell_i:\\; y=m_i x +\\bigl(n-i-m_i(i+1)\\bigr).\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nEquation (4) is obtained by forcing \\(\\ell_i\\) to pass through \\(P_i\\).  \nBecause the slopes \\(m_i\\) are distinct, the lines \\(\\ell_i\\) are distinct and none of them is horizontal, vertical or diagonal; therefore they are sunny.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**(c) Verification of the covering property.**  \n\nLet \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal T_n\\).\n\n*If \\(b\\le n-k-1\\)*, then the horizontal line \\(y=b\\) (one of the \\(L_h^{(j)}\\)) contains \\((a,b)\\).\n\n*If \\(b\\ge n-k\\) and \\(a=1\\)*, the point lies on the vertical line \\(x=1\\).\n\n*If \\(b\\ge n-k\\) and \\(a\\ge2\\)*, then by th